  "InputApiHint": "Legacy DirectInput 7. Best with a pad connected directly and nothing in between: a PS4 pad over USB has the same numbering as the Logitech Rumblepad 2 the PC controls were made for. Tested Nov 2026: DS4Windows (with HidHide / VIIPER / USBip drivers) made the game crash in DINPUT.dll; dinputto8 stopped the crash but broke the team-select screen. After removing DS4Windows and its drivers, the raw pad works fully without dinputto8. Pause is Esc; special moves are L1 + a face button.",
  "Notes": "HB Studios engine shared with Cricket 07; Direct3D 8 (the community widescreen fix ships dgVoodoo2's d3d8.dll - the app confirms from the exe). Resolution is stored as two little-endian 16-bit values (width, height) in the binary .pro profile in Documents\\EA SPORTS(TM) Rugby 08; the offset differs between profiles, so the Game config tab searches for it. Forum users report changing in-game display options can reset it to 1024x768. A freeze at the start-up screen has been reported, sometimes from antivirus - add an exception if so. Widescreen needs the community fix (you install it yourself).",
  "DrmNotes": "Listed on PCGamingWiki's SafeDisc page (version not given). SafeDisc's secdrv.sys driver is disabled on Windows 10/11, so the disc check cannot run there. No official DRM-free or digital re-release is known. This launcher only reports SafeDisc - it never removes or bypasses it. Don't run 'replacement exe' files from forums: they are unverified and can carry malware.",
